    "result_text": "The full suite is green (AcceptanceBase and AuditLogCapture are support classes, not tests). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is rejected with **409** when the target city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` / `EnsureUniqueHousehold` guards), I added:\n\n- **`EnsureCityHasCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a single-responsibility guard step reading the shared `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, counting existing owners in the same city (trimmed, case-insensitive) via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throwing when the count reaches the capacity of 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** \u2014 a checked exception carrying the offending city and capacity.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail`, reusing the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper like the other handlers.\n- Wired the new step into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureUniqueHousehold` and `normalizeEmail`, with `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with the rest of the pipeline.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` passes and the full `mvn test` build is green.",
